+## When `beforeSession` throws
+
+- A `beforeSession` that throws reaches the same `catch` and `finally` as any other failure in the turn: the caller is still rejected with the error it threw, `onError` fires with the session and that error, then `afterSession` runs. What `afterSession` receives there is the session exactly as `beforeSession` left it — no provider call was made and no entry was appended — so a cleanup hook can tell "never allocated" from "allocated and finished" from the session alone ([validated by: runs onError then afterSession and still rejects the caller when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L34)).
+
